{%- set card = 'meter-gbm' -%}
{%- set title = 'the meter model: gbm over the household clusters, reconciled' -%}
{% set intended %}
The meter model forecasts the hourly load of each of the {{ v('meter.clusters') }} load shape clusters
and of the panel total for a fixed panel of {{ v('meter.forecast.households') }} London households,
1 to {{ v('policy.horizons') }} hours ahead of a daily origin, reconciled to the total by MinT. It is
the second hierarchy in the build and is meant to show bottom up forecasting at the meter and what
reconciliation does to it. It is not meant for any live tariff, for households outside the panel,
for 2026, or for half hourly settlement.
{% endset %}
{% set data %}
The Low Carbon London release ({{ v('data.london.rows') }} readings, {{ v('data.london.households') }}
households, {{ v('data.london.first') }} to {{ v('data.london.last') }}), read through DuckDB; the
{{ v('meter.forecast.households') }} households reporting through the whole forecast window
({{ v('meter.forecast.household_share') }} of those profiled), summed hourly per cluster and in total.
No weather. Test period {{ v('meter.forecast.test_start') }} to {{ v('meter.forecast.test_end') }}, the
year before as validation.
{% endset %}
{% set fit %}
The gbm backend on the cluster panel as if the clusters were authorities: one booster with the
quantile objective at the five levels, {{ v('meter.forecast.fits') }} fits over
{{ v('meter.forecast.origins') }} origins, conformalized on the validation year; MinT with the shrunk
covariance of the calibration model's validation residuals (intensity
{{ v('meter.forecast.shrinkage_intensity') }}). Hourly rather than half hourly because the
forecasting interface is hourly (`DECISIONS.md`).
{% endset %}
{% set metrics %}
{{ table('meter.forecast.by_level') }}

{{ label('meter.forecast.by_level') }}

MinT {{ v('meter.forecast.mint_verdict_total') }} at the total ({{ v('meter.forecast.mint_gain_total') }}
points of MAPE) and {{ v('meter.forecast.mint_verdict_clusters') }} at the clusters
({{ v('meter.forecast.mint_gain_clusters') }}); coherence gaps bottom up
{{ v('meter.forecast.coherence_gap.bottom_up') }} kWh and MinT {{ v('meter.forecast.coherence_gap.mint') }} kWh.
{% endset %}
{% set contract %}
- [x] **trained**: {{ v('meter.forecast.fits') }} fits over {{ v('meter.forecast.origins') }} origins.
- [x] **timed**: part of the meter stage's {{ v('meter.seconds') }} seconds.
- [x] **calibrated**: conformalized on the validation year; 90 percent coverage {{ v('meter.forecast.base.level0.coverage_90') }} at the total on test.
- [x] **useful**: MAPE {{ v('meter.forecast.base.level0.mape') }} at the total before reconciliation and {{ v('meter.forecast.mint.level0.mape') }} after.
- [ ] **fair**: not applicable; the clusters are load shapes, not people, and no household identifier is published.
- [ ] **gated**: not built; the registry's gates judge the grid backends, and the meter model is not served.
- [ ] **served**: not applicable; the meter model is an analysis, not an API route.
- [ ] **integrated**: not applicable, as above.
- [ ] **monitored**: not applicable; there is no live meter feed.
- [x] **documented**: this card and `docs/meter.md`.
- [x] **bounded**: the intended use above; the fixed panel and the hourly resolution are stated.
- [x] **validated**: coherence to the kilowatt hour and accuracy before and after by level with block bootstrap intervals.
- [x] **explainable at the decision**: the clusters are described by shape and share; the reconciled total is beside the base one at every origin in `results/meter/forecast_total.parquet`.
{% endset %}
{% set limitations %}
A fixed panel of {{ v('meter.forecast.households') }} households is a stated subsample of the release.
No weather, so the winter of 2013 to 2014 is forecast from lags and the calendar alone. Hourly, not
half hourly. Three months of test is a short year. The households opted in a decade ago.
{% endset %}
